  "trend_comparison_note": "Least-squares fit vs Page-Hinkley on identical inputs. Neither is claimed as novel; Choi et al. (2026) published Page-Hinkley for this problem. Finding: the two methods win on different sampling regimes. The windowed fit is faster on densely sampled cameras (76 s vs 184 s, 789 s vs 971 s), while Page-Hinkley is faster on sparsely sampled ones (4500 s vs 5400 s) because it is sample-based rather than time-based. An earlier fixed 300 s window caused the fit to fail completely on a camera sampled every 15 minutes; the window is now adaptive."
}